{
  "name": "Telegram assistant: /weather",
  "meta": {
    "description": "A Telegram bot that answers /weather <city> with the current weather and forecast (Open-Meteo, no key). Works without a public URL."
  },
  "nodes": [
    {
      "id": "trigger",
      "name": "On /weather",
      "type": "flowforge.telegramTrigger",
      "typeVersion": 1,
      "position": [
        0,
        0
      ],
      "parameters": {
        "updates": [
          "message"
        ],
        "options": {
          "command": "/weather"
        }
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "weather",
      "name": "Weather",
      "type": "flowforge.openMeteo",
      "typeVersion": 1,
      "position": [
        280,
        0
      ],
      "onError": "continueErrorOutput",
      "parameters": {
        "operation": "getWeather",
        "locationMode": "city",
        "city": "={{ $json.args || 'Paris' }}",
        "include": [
          "current",
          "daily"
        ],
        "forecastDays": 3
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "reply",
      "name": "Reply",
      "type": "flowforge.telegram",
      "typeVersion": 1,
      "position": [
        560,
        -90
      ],
      "parameters": {
        "operation": "sendMessage",
        "chatId": "={{ $('On /weather').item.json.chatId }}",
        "text": "={{ $json.summary }}\n\n{{ $json.daily.map((d) => d.emoji + ' ' + d.date + ': ' + d.temperatureMin + ' to ' + d.temperatureMax + ' ' + $json.units.temperature).join('\\n') }}",
        "parseMode": "none"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "sorry",
      "name": "Reply not found",
      "type": "flowforge.telegram",
      "typeVersion": 1,
      "position": [
        560,
        110
      ],
      "parameters": {
        "operation": "sendMessage",
        "chatId": "={{ $('On /weather').item.json.chatId }}",
        "text": "=🤔 I could not find \"{{ $('On /weather').item.json.args }}\". Try: /weather Paris",
        "parseMode": "none"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "note",
      "name": "How to use",
      "type": "flowforge.stickyNote",
      "typeVersion": 1,
      "position": [
        -60,
        -330
      ],
      "parameters": {
        "content": "## Telegram assistant\n1. Create a bot with **@BotFather** (`/newbot`) and copy the token.\n2. **Credentials**: add a **Telegram Bot** credential, or set `TELEGRAM_BOT_TOKEN` in `.env`.\n3. Switch the workflow to **Active**.\n4. In Telegram, open your bot, press **Start**, then send `/weather Paris`.\n5. To test in the editor instead: open **On /weather** → *Listen for test event*, then send the command.\n\nOnly one program can read a bot: do not use the same bot in n8n at the same time.",
        "width": 580,
        "height": 260,
        "color": 4
      }
    }
  ],
  "connections": {
    "On /weather": {
      "main": [
        [
          {
            "node": "Weather",
            "type": "main",
            "index": 0
          }
        ]
      ]
    },
    "Weather": {
      "main": [
        [
          {
            "node": "Reply",
            "type": "main",
            "index": 0
          }
        ],
        [
          {
            "node": "Reply not found",
            "type": "main",
            "index": 0
          }
        ]
      ]
    }
  },
  "settings": {}
}
